{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785702263,"nonce":"qPG7DBAtmXc2uTDYTtUh4SgZ3G4=","title":"Gates the packing ADR (see the sibling ticket). Decided 2026-08-03 (grill; ADR-0066).","message":"**The cold flush is unmeasured.** The 2026-08-02 benchmark (`crates/scarab-workspace-client/tests/feed_cost.rs`, git-bug `4ce7f2c`) measured the client→Depot legs — `materialize` 0.54 ms/file, `ingest` 2.68 ms/file. It never measured `flush_to_cold`, the **Depot→object-storage** leg. That leg:\n\n- is a separate ~50k requests for a 50k-file workspace,\n- runs against real object storage rather than the loopback store the benchmark used,\n- and **gates `Succeeded`** per ADR-0064.\n\nSo the leg most likely to benefit from packing is the one with no number.\n\n- [ ] Extend the existing harness with the flush leg (it already spins a real router + real client; add the Depot→cold hop)\n- [ ] Run against something with realistic per-request latency, not a loopback store — state the RTT used and how it was chosen\n- [ ] Report per-file cost and total for 250 / 2000 files, and extrapolate to 50k, in the same shape as the 4ce7f2c table so the numbers are comparable\n- [ ] Report the split between the probe pass (HEADs) and the uploads (PUTs), since the presence index would remove the former and packing the latter\n- [ ] State the bias honestly, as 4ce7f2c did","files":null}]}